Let me do that calculation: 23 minus 20. Hmm, 23 minus 20 is 3. So, after using 20 apples, they have 3 apples remaining. 

Then, they bought 6 more apples. So, now I need to add those 6 apples to the remaining 3 apples. That would be 3 plus 6. Let me calculate that: 3 + 6 equals 9. 

Wait, is that all? Let me check again. Starting with 23, subtract 20 gives 3. Then adding 6 gives 9. Yeah, that seems right. 

But let me make sure I didn't miss any steps. The problem says they used 20 to make lunch, then bought 6 more. So, the order is important here. First, they use some apples, then they buy more. So the operations are subtraction followed by addition. 

