Alternatively, maybe someone could think that they have 23 apples, use 20, then add 6. So 23 - 20 = 3, then 3 + 6 = 9. So the answer is 9. 

I don't see any other operations involved here. The problem is straightforward. They didn't mention any other apples being taken away or added. So I think 9 is the correct answer. 

Just to confirm, if I have 23 apples, use 20, you have 3 left. Then adding 6 more, so 3 + 6 = 9. Yes. 

So, the final answer should be 9. 

