$$
41 \text{ (regular sodas)} + 22 \text{ (diet sodas)} = 63 \text{ sodas}
$$

Next, we are told that **each shelf can hold 9 sodas**. To find out how many shelves are needed, we divide the total number of sodas by the capacity of a single shelf:

$$
63 \div 9 = 7
$$

---

Thus, Jerry would fill up **7 shelves** with the sodas.

