Megan initially baked 71 cupcakes. After her brother Todd ate 43 of them, the number of cupcakes left is $ 71 - 43 = 28 $.

To determine how many packages Megan can make, we divide the remaining cupcakes by the number of cupcakes per package:
$$
28 \div 7 = 4
$$

Thus, Megan can make $\boxed{4}$ packages. 
