Now, they want to use these 54 apples to make pies. Each pie requires 6 apples. So I need to divide the remaining apples by the number of apples per pie. That would be 54 divided by 6. Let me calculate that. 6 times 9 is 54, so 54 divided by 6 equals 9. 

So, they can make 9 pies. Let me check my steps again. Subtract the apples given out from the total: 96-42=54. Then divide by 6: 54/6=9. Yep, that seems right. I don't think I made any mistakes here. The answer should be 9.
