The cafeteria started with 96 apples. After giving out 42 apples to students, the remaining number of apples is calculated as follows:

$$
96 - 42 = 54
$$

Each pie requires 6 apples. To find out how many pies can be made, divide the remaining apples by the number of apples per pie:

$$
54 \div 6 = 9
$$

Thus, the number of pies that can be made is $\boxed{9}$. 
