First, I need to figure out how many books Adam has after selling 11. So he started with 33, sold 11. That would be 33 minus 11. Let me do that subtraction: 33 - 11 = 22. So after selling, he has 22 books left.

Now, he uses the money from selling those 11 books to buy 23 new books. Wait, does that mean he buys 23 new books with the money he got from selling 11? So, he's replacing some books with new ones? But he sold 11, so he had 22 left. Then he buys 23 new ones. So does that mean he adds 23 to his remaining 22? So total books would be 22 + 23 = 45?

