Will worked at a grocery store and earns $8 per hour. On Monday, he worked 8 hours, and on Tuesday, he worked 2 hours. To calculate his total earnings over the two days, we first compute his earnings for each day separately and then add them together.

On Monday, his earnings are:
$$
8 \text{ hours} \times 8 \text{ dollars/hour} = 64 \text{ dollars}
$$

On Tuesday, his earnings are:
$$
2 \text{ hours} \times 8 \text{ dollars/hour} = 16 \text{ dollars}
$$

Adding both days' earnings:
$$
64 \text{ dollars} + 16 \text{ dollars} = 80 \text{ dollars}
$$

Alternatively, we can calculate the total hours worked:
$$
8 \text{ hours} + 2 \text{ hours} = 10 \text{ hours}
$$

Then calculate the total earnings:
$$
10 \text{ hours} \times 8 \text{ dollars/hour} = 80 \text{ dollars}
$$

Thus, Will made a total of $\boxed{80}$ dollars over the two days. The calculations are consistent and correct. The final answer is \boxed{80}. 

\boxed{80}  
