To determine how much money Will made over the two days, we start by analyzing the information given:

- Will earns **$8 per hour**.
- On **Monday**, he worked **8 hours**.
- On **Tuesday**, he worked **2 hours**.

---

### Step 1: Calculate earnings for Monday
$$
\text{Earnings on Monday} = 8 \text{ hours} \times 8 \text{ dollars/hour} = 64 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate earnings for Tuesday
$$
\text{Earnings on Tuesday} = 2 \text{ hours} \times 8 \text{ dollars/hour} = 16 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Step 3: Calculate total earnings
$$
\text{Total earnings} = \text{Earnings on Monday} + \text{Earnings on Tuesday} = 64 + 16 = 80 \text{ dollars}
$$

We can also verify by adding the total hours worked:
$$
\text{Total hours} = 8 + 2 = 10 \text{ hours}
$$
$$
\text{Total earnings} = 10 \times 8 = 80 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Final Answer
$$
\boxed{80}
$$

